Description: avfilter/tonemap: reshape each Dolby Vision component with the piece its own value picks
 An RPU can split the reshaping curve of each component into up to eight
 pieces at pivots. The base-layer value of a component picks the piece
 for that component. tonemapx and tonemap_cuda chose a piece for I only.
 They wrote only the pivots of I into their reshaping buffer, and they
 reshaped P and T with the first piece over the whole range.
 .
 On a synthetic profile 5 picture of flat patches, with P and T in two
 polynomial pieces, 626 of 753 checked patches came out more than one
 code from the definition, up to 50 luma and 61 chroma codes. With three
 second-order pieces, 708 of 726 came out wrong, up to 109 chroma codes.
 .
 Write the pivots of every component, and choose the piece of P and T as
 the filters choose the piece of I. In tonemapx the C loop does this,
 and on the SSE4.2, AVX2 and NEON paths dovi_piece_coeffs() does. In
 tonemap_cuda the reshape kernel does this, for the direct kernels and
 for the 3D lookup table. A component with one piece takes the same path
 as before.
Author: Streamarr
Forwarded: no
